  "result": "Perfect! All 357 tests pass, including the 10 new tests for `mergeCustomers`. The implementation is complete and working correctly.\n\nHere's a summary of what was added:\n\n**In `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added `SAME_CUSTOMER` error code for when attempting to merge a customer with itself\n\n**In `src/customers.js`:**\n- Added `mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)` function that:\n  - Normalizes both customer IDs\n  - Returns `SAME_CUSTOMER` error if both IDs are identical\n  - Returns `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` if either customer doesn't exist\n  - Removes the `fromId` customer from the customers array\n  - Updates all invoices belonging to `fromId` to belong to `intoId`\n  - Returns `ok({ customers, invoices })` with the updated arrays\n  - Doesn't mutate the input arrays\n\n**In `test/customers.test.js`:**\n- Added 10 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Basic merge functionality\n  - Error cases (missing customers, same customer)\n  - ID normalization (lowercase, spaces)\n  - Non-mutation of inputs\n  - Various invoice scenarios (empty list, multiple invoices)",
